  ("Can a heat pump use the ductwork in my older Cambridge home?", "Often it can, but only after an airflow test. Heat pumps need more airflow per ton than old furnaces did, so we measure static pressure first and fix or supplement the ducts if they fall short."),
  ("What's the best option for a stone house in Galt with no ducts?", "A ductless or multi-zone heat pump is usually the best fit. Each indoor head needs only a small opening through the wall, and the system heats and cools without new ductwork."),
